card.statement:
Let $R$ be as above and let $X, X^\prime \in \rmT_\bbF/\sim_{R}$ with antidominant weights $\Lambda\in X$, $\Lambda^\prime \in X^\prime$. If $\Lambda, \Lambda^\prime$ are compatible and satisfy the condition <<ref:WeylCha>> and $\Stab_R(\Lambda) \subset \Stab_R(\Lambda^\prime)$, then

\[ 	\xymatrix{
\calZ_{R,X} \ar[r]^-{\widesim{}} &  \calZ_{R,X^\prime}^{\bigoplus |\Stab_R(\Lambda^\prime)/\Stab_R(\Lambda)|}	}
\]

as $\calZ_{R,X^\prime}$-modules. Moreover, there exists a natural embedding of $R$-algebras $\calZ_{R,X^\prime} \rightarrow \calZ_{R,X}$ sending each $z\in \calZ_{R,X^\prime}$ to the $|\Stab_R(\Lambda^\prime)/\Stab_R(\Lambda)|$-copies of $z$ in $\calZ_{R,X}$, in the sense of the above isomorphism.
